1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Signalbox: governed actions for AI agents.
A walkthrough of saved, real local evidence.

2
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:15,000
The agent proposes an action. Signalbox authorizes it.
A separate worker records the resulting effect.

3
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Nemotron Ultra and Super edited a disposable website
and passed its check in Nebius Sandbox.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Production was denied. Nano first recommended human review.
That recommendation did not create an approval request.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:43,000
Studio separates action evidence from policy editing.
This reviewer cannot activate or roll back policy.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:50,000
A separate same-input proof verified allowed, denied,
and allowed again after policy rollback.

7
00:00:50,000 --> 00:01:00,000
We continued the saved run with an explicit staging alternative.
One additional Nano request selected retryStaging.

8
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Signalbox authorized staging. After fixing a missing dispatch input,
the worker succeeded without another model or Sandbox call.

9
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:20,000
This is the actual published file, with its digest verified.
The effect is local staging; the hosted instance is unchanged.
